  "notes": "{煮|に}える describes food reaching a state of being fully cooked in boiling liquid.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{煮|に}る→煮る：01971_niru⟧ (transitive, to cook/boil something)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{煮|に}えて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means 'is cooked/done' (resulting state). Example: ⟦{野菜|やさい}→野菜：02265_yasai⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{煮|に}えて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ (the vegetables are cooked).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{野菜|やさい}→野菜：02265_yasai⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{煮|に}える: vegetables get cooked\n- ⟦よく→よく：00601_yoku⟧{煮|に}える: to cook thoroughly\n- ⟦まだ→まだ：00603_mada⟧{煮|に}えて⟦いない→いる：00495_iru⟧: not cooked yet\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{煮|に}て→煮る：01971_niru⟧⟦も→も：00484_mo⟧⟦{焼|や}いても→焼く：01123_yaku⟧⟦{食|く}えない→食う：02657_kuu⟧: someone impossible to deal with (lit. 'can't eat whether boiled or grilled')\n- ⟦{業|ごう}→業：noentry⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{煮|に}やす→煮やす：noentry⟧: to lose patience",
